From: Yaron Shahrabani <yarons@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: Application control of the software ISP autofocus, Android support

Soft IPA: the lens controls are passed to init() as well, so that the Af
algorithm can register AfMode, AfTrigger and LensPosition for cameras with
a focus lens. Manual mode positions the lens with LensPosition (0.0 far to
10.0 near, mapped linearly to the lens positions "farPosition" and
"macroPosition" of the tuning file: the lens is not calibrated), auto mode
searches when triggered, continuous mode (the default) as before, and a
trigger holds the focus until it is cancelled. AfState and LensPosition are
reported in the metadata.

Android HAL, for cameras with controls::AfMode: AF modes OFF, AUTO,
CONTINUOUS_VIDEO and CONTINUOUS_PICTURE, one AF region (the measurement
stays in the centre for now), minimum focus distance from LensPosition,
continuous AF in the request templates, AF_MODE / AF_TRIGGER /
LENS_FOCUS_DISTANCE translated to the libcamera controls, AF_STATE and
LENS_FOCUS_DISTANCE and the AF regions of the request (applications wait for
them) in the results. The test pattern and face detection modes are only set for
cameras that have it (it logged an error for every request).

The HAL no longer forgets the settings of the first request of a session:
lastSettings_ was reset right after it had been set from that request, which
left every following request of a repeating request without settings.
